<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The plan editor: the drawing, what is selected on it, and the quantities that come off it.

  Translators, three things this file will not bend on:

  1. Anything that distinguishes *measured* from *derived* is load-bearing, not hedging. A
     distance drawn on the plan, a room placed by hand, a corner the solver squared up —
     each says so because the alternative is a number the user trusts more than it deserves
     (docs/PRODUCT_PLAN.md §5). Keep the qualification even where it makes a sentence longer.
  2. The quantities are advice with a reason attached. "Check the tin" and "raise it for a
     diagonal lay" are the parts that stop somebody ordering the wrong amount.
  3. `editor_wall_help` and `editor_ceiling_help` explain a feature that is otherwise
     invisible — typing a tape measurement, and looking up while capturing. They are the only
     place either is taught.
-->
